		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://ventureburn.com/?p=203900</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Electric vehicle sales made up more than 25% of the total vehicle sales in 2025 as more people go green. Taking a different route, Revoy raises $27 million on a</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/revoy-raises-27-million-electric-truck-dolly/" data-wpel-link="internal">Revoy Raises $27 Million to Turn Old Diesel Trucks Into Hybrids</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Electric vehicle sales made up more than 25% of the </span><a href="https://www.iea.org/reports/global-ev-outlook-2026/trends-in-electric-cars" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">total vehicle sales</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> in 2025 as more people go green. Taking a different route, Revoy raises $27 million on a bet that trucking companies can go electric without replacing old trucks. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Standard Capital led the round, with XYZ Venture Capital, Doerr Capital, Time Ventures, Y Combinator, Leap Ventures, and Y Combinator co-founder Paul Graham also putting money in. Combined with earlier rounds, the San Francisco company has now raised $41 million.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The idea is almost mechanically simple: a powered dolly slots between a truck’s cab and its trailer, and the diesel engine gets an electric assist instead of a replacement. Without the need for a new truck or even rewiring, dependence is on a device that clips onto a standard fifth-wheel hitch in minutes.</span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">How the Revoy Dolly Actually Works</span></h2>
<div id="attachment_203902" style="width: 1034px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203902" class="size-large wp-image-203902" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Revoy-Dolly-1024x682.jpeg" alt="Side profile of a white and black standalone Revoy EV unit with small front landing wheels and an exposed rear chassis, parked in a sunny desert landscape under a clear blue sky." width="1024" height="682" /><p id="caption-attachment-203902" class="wp-caption-text">Revoy Dolly</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The </span><a href="https://www.revoy.com/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">Revoy dolly</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> carries its own motor and a 575-kilowatt-hour battery. This is about the size you’d find in a fully electric semi. The battery helps to push the truck forward through its own powered axle. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">On a full charge, it can carry a loaded 36-tonne rig more than 200 miles while cutting diesel use by up to 95% and emissions by up to 85%, according to the company. Regenerative braking recovers energy on the way down and, as a side effect, shortens stopping distance by as much as 30%.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Revoy built it to require zero modification to the truck or trailer it’s attached to. The dolly reads the driver’s throttle and brake inputs, adds torque during acceleration, and switches to charging mode under braking. Interestingly, it does all these without the driver’s input. It also carries its own driver-assistance features, including blind-spot detection and rollover correction.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/simile-raises-200-million-agentic-twin-consumer-simulations/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Simile Raises $200M for Building Agentic Twin Simulations</i></b></a></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">The Pitch: Compete With Diesel on Price</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Battery-electric semis exist, but they’re expensive and fleets replace trucks slowly, which has kept most heavy-duty freight running on diesel. Revoy intends to let go of the purchase completely. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Since the company owns the dollies and leases them by the mile, a trucking company is charged with keeping its existing diesel tractors and pays only for the miles it runs electric.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">CEO Peter Reinhardt first created and later decided to sell the customer-data company Segment to Twilio for $3.2 billion. He says that the technology allows for competition with diesel and no other electric truck in the US can boast of this just yet. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Co-founder and CTO Ian Rust, Revoy’s first hire and a former early engineer at self-driving startup Cruise, has described the approach more bluntly: instead of removing the driver, Revoy is using robotics to swap the fuel source.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/k2-space-raises-500m-6-8-billion-valuation/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>K2 Space Raises $500M To Scale Large, High-Power Satellites</i></b></a></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">What the Money Actually Builds</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Revoy plans to start commercial service later this year on a roughly 200-mile freight route near Portland, Oregon, running four dollies assembled from components sourced in China. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">It might seem like a small start, but it’s deliberate. Reinhardt has said a single commercially viable lane needs around two dozen dollies, a manufacturing volume the company thinks it can hit without needing to scale up first.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Some of the new funding will go into building a second-generation dolly with a smaller, cheaper battery pack that still hits the same 200-plus-mile range. </span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/cisco-backed-eliyan-raises-145m-at-1b-valuation/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Eliyan Raises $145 Milli to Fix AI’s Data Bottleneck</i></b></a></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/revoy-raises-27-million-electric-truck-dolly/" data-wpel-link="internal">Revoy Raises $27 Million to Turn Old Diesel Trucks Into Hybrids</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
