					<description><![CDATA[<p>Funding Fuels Platform Expansion And AI Development The New York-based alternative investment platform CAIS raised $170 million in Series D financing that will support the enhancement of the firm&#8217;s technology</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/cais-raises-170m/" data-wpel-link="internal">CAIS Raises $170M At $2 Billion Valuation To Expand Alternative Investment Platform</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<h2><b>Funding Fuels Platform Expansion And AI Development</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The New York-based alternative investment platform CAIS raised $170 million in Series D financing that will support the enhancement of the firm&#8217;s technology platform and fuel expansion. The investment values the firm at $2 billion and brings its total funds raised to almost $600 million.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The round was conducted with Vista Equity Partners as the lead investor along with AllianzBernstein, Blue Owl Capital, Carlyle, Fortress Investment Group, Golub Capital, Lord Abbett, and the Royal Bank of Canada. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The proceeds will be used to scale the CAIS platform, enhance its AI capabilities, pursue additional strategic growth opportunities, and continue building tools to simplify financial advisor access and allocation to alternatives.</span></p>
<h2><b>Platform Growth Reflects Rising Advisor Demand</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Since its founding in 2009, CAIS has established an end-to-end infrastructure and operating system that can support alternative investments throughout the entire life cycle-from an initial investment assessment and commitment through reporting and management. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">In total, CAIS&#8217; platform powersmore than2,500 wealth management firms, amounting to more than 65,000 financial advisors. The advisory firms that work with CAIS manage on average about $8.5 trillion in client assets, indicating the breadth of the CAIS network.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company reported substantial operating strength over the first half of 2026, with transaction volume increasing 53% year-over-year and total platform assets increasing 55%. 2026&#8217;s first-half organic revenue growth rate three-year average was 37%.</span></p>
<h2><b>AI And Technology Drive Future Strategy<br />
</b></h2>
<div id="attachment_203869" style="width: 1322px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203869" class="size-full wp-image-203869" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/a-futuristic-poster-depicting-a-holograp_X0ziWUCTVsml12Wsf95o5Q_2nKRFO2xSXmJPyqXclwkrw.png" alt="A neon futuristic visual showing an AI-powered platform for managing alternative investments and advisor workflows." width="1312" height="736" /><p id="caption-attachment-203869" class="wp-caption-text">CAIS integrates AI to simplify alternative investing and boost advisor productivity. Source: Created by Ventureburn</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">CAIS aims to serve as the platform of choice for advisors on alternative investing. Stretching from Funds Marketplace and Custom Funds to Capital Markets, it creates a single digital space for advisors to source, assess, invest in, and service private market private equity products.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">AI is an increasingly central pillar of that effort. The organization is integrating AI into its advisor workflow, aiming to save time and increase advisor productivity, and automate tasks involved in how advisors analyze an investment in the first place.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The growing adoption of private market assets among wealth managers has created increasing demand for platforms capable of handling complex investment products while maintaining compliance and operational efficiency. CAIS aims to address that need through continued technology development and product expansion.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">More News: <a href="https://ventureburn.com/commonwealth-fusion-systems-raises-1-billion/" data-wpel-link="internal">Commonwealth Fusion Systems Raises $1 Billion To Advance Commercial Fusion Power</a></span></p>
<h2><b>Investors Back Long-Term Alternative Investment Infrastructure</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The new funding reveals a large increase in institutional belief in alternative infrastructure over and above the assets. As more and more independents use alternatives such as private equity, private credit, </span><a href="https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/hedgefund.asp" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">hedge funds</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> and alternative assets, platforms that streamline investment workflows have been deemed more critical to them.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The new $170m financing represents one of the biggest Series D funds in the U.S over the last few years, the industry said. Also significant is that large global asset managers are still eager to support tech firms enabling the ever-growing private wealth industry.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">CAIS aims to use the money to continue developing and funding infrastructure and artificial intelligence features and further drive business growth as it remains a key technology partner for wealth managers. CAIS is backed with over $600m in capital.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">To stay updated on crypto venture capital funding and market trends, visit our </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/category/news/venture-capital/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">venture capital news section</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> for more insights.</span></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/cais-raises-170m/" data-wpel-link="internal">CAIS Raises $170M At $2 Billion Valuation To Expand Alternative Investment Platform</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
